(## Restoring Expanded State After A Server Redirect) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(TIS is server-rendered FastAPI/Jinja, not an SPA, so expand/collapse state) Tj
T*
(\(native `<details>`, dialogs\) lives only in the DOM and is normally lost the) Tj
T*
(moment an action redirects to a fresh render. The sanctioned fix reuses two) Tj
T*
(things that already existed rather than introducing a new mechanism: the) Tj
T*
(existing `return_to` form-field/query-param convention, and its `#fragment`) Tj
T*
(preservation already built into `redirect_utils.redirect_with_notice\(\)` /) Tj
T*
(`redirect_with_error\(\)` \(moved out of `main.py` so any router can share the) Tj
T*
(same open-redirect guard, `redirect_utils.safe_redirect_path\(\)`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A route that wants the user to land back on a specific element accepts a) Tj
T*
(`return_to` value shaped `<path>[?query]#<element-id>`, validates it with) Tj
T*
(`redirect_utils.safe_redirect_path\(return_to, default=<page path>\)`, and) Tj
T*
(redirects there. The shared client script `static/js/reopen-on-load.js`,) Tj
T*
(loaded globally from `base.html`, runs on `DOMContentLoaded`, resolves a) Tj
T*
(target id from `window.location.hash` \(or an optional inline) Tj
T*
(`window.__tisReopenTargetId` a page can render for a non-redirect, in-place) Tj
T*
(response\), and if the matching element is a `<details>`, opens it and scrolls) Tj
T*
(it into view. A missing, stale, or renamed id is a silent no-op by design -) Tj
T*
(`document.getElementById` never throws, so this can never break a page load.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Do not invent a page-local variant of this pattern. Give the element to) Tj
T*
(reopen a stable, predictable id, pass `return_to` through the existing) Tj
T*
(convention, and let the shared script do the reopening. Planning's Remove) Tj
T*
(Demand action \(`routers/planning.py:delete_planning_subject_demand`\) is the) Tj
T*
(reference implementation.) Tj
