() Tj
T*
(# TIS Rejected Architectural Decisions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This document records significant ideas that were considered and rejected. It helps future) Tj
T*
(developers and AI assistants avoid reopening old decisions without new evidence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected decisions are not failures. They are part of the design record.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Single Application For Landing And Portal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date:) Tj
T*
(2026-06-26) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Context:) Tj
T*
(TIS needs both a public marketing site and a protected operational app. The public site) Tj
T*
(needs premium storytelling and conversion design; the app needs authenticated academic) Tj
T*
(operations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proposed solution:) Tj
T*
(Use the FastAPI/Jinja app for both the public landing website and the operational portal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why rejected:) Tj
T*
(The two surfaces have different runtimes, audiences, design needs, deployment concerns, and) Tj
T*
(risk profiles. Mixing them would make backend/operational tasks more likely to accidentally) Tj
T*
(change the public website.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Chosen solution:) Tj
T*
(Keep `tis-landing-website/` as a separate Next.js public landing website and keep the) Tj
T*
(FastAPI app as the operational portal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Long-term consequences:) Tj
T*
(Developers must respect the landing/portal boundary. Landing changes require explicit) Tj
T*
(approval and must use the Next.js source of truth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Stripe Instead Of Paddle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date:) Tj
T*
(2026-06-26) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Context:) Tj
T*
(TIS needs subscription payment collection, billing state, and future subscription lifecycle) Tj
T*
(workflows.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proposed solution:) Tj
T*
(Use Stripe as the payment provider.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why rejected:) Tj
T*
