(## Documentation Without ADRs) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date:) Tj
T*
(2026-06-26) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Context:) Tj
T*
(TIS decisions span SaaS identity, payments, provisioning, landing architecture, and KMS) Tj
T*
(governance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proposed solution:) Tj
T*
(Keep only a master context and change history.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why rejected:) Tj
T*
(Chronological history does not explain major decision tradeoffs deeply enough. Future) Tj
T*
(developers would repeatedly reopen settled architecture questions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Chosen solution:) Tj
T*
(Maintain ADRs under `docs/adr/` for major accepted decisions and this rejected-decision) Tj
T*
(record for important alternatives.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Long-term consequences:) Tj
T*
(Major decisions require explicit traceability. ADRs and rejected decisions must be updated) Tj
T*
(when architecture changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Weak Generic Landing Page Design) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date:) Tj
T*
(2026-06-26) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Context:) Tj
T*
(The public landing website is the first impression for schools evaluating TIS.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proposed solution:) Tj
T*
(Use a generic SaaS layout with vague claims, weak fake 3D visuals, or internal) Tj
T*
(implementation language.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why rejected:) Tj
T*
(TIS needs credibility with school leaders. Generic visuals and internal language reduce) Tj
T*
(trust and do not communicate academic operations value.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Chosen solution:) Tj
T*
(Use premium storytelling, strong visual assets, clear customer language, and the separate) Tj
T*
(Next.js landing visual system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Long-term consequences:) Tj
T*
(Landing work should be deliberate, visually strong, and customer-facing. Avoid terms like) Tj
T*
(tenant, provisioning, and internal milestone labels.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
