() Tj
T*
(# TIS Project Governance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This document defines how TIS engineering decisions, approvals, documentation, and quality) Tj
T*
(gates should be governed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Ownership Model) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Product/project ownership:) Tj
T*
(Defines business direction, roadmap priorities, customer experience, and approval for major) Tj
T*
(changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Platform Owner:) Tj
T*
(Owns platform-level operations, platform accounts, provisioning oversight, and KMS) Tj
T*
(visibility.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Engineering implementer:) Tj
T*
(Human developer, Codex, or ChatGPT-assisted coding session responsible for scoped) Tj
T*
(implementation and validation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reviewer:) Tj
T*
(Reviews implementation, KMS updates, risk boundaries, and validation results.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Approved Development Agents And Master Orchestration) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The approved development-agent pool is Codex, Claude Code, and Cline/ClinePass.) Tj
T*
(Cline is the coding agent; ClinePass is its provider/subscription choice, not a) Tj
T*
(separate fourth agent. All three follow AGENTS.md and the same governing KMS,) Tj
T*
(safety boundaries, KIA, validation, and explicit release authorization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The master TIS conversation allocates bounded tasks by complexity, specialization,) Tj
T*
(risk, independent-review value, and current usage/load. Reassess allocation per) Tj
T*
(task and rebalance so one or two agents are not unnecessarily overloaded. Avoid) Tj
T*
(permanent module ownership or rigid agent assignments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Preferred tendencies, not hard walls:) Tj
T*
(- Codex: primary implementation and broad repository changes.) Tj
T*
(- Claude Code: deep investigation, architecture, complex business logic, and a) Tj
T*
(  second implementation path.) Tj
T*
(- ClinePass: independent implementation, verification, regression/safety review,) Tj
T*
(  workflow consistency, and any suitable task as a third capable developer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Choose a different author/reviewer where independent review adds value. Handoffs) Tj
T*
(state scope, acceptance criteria, forbidden files, current worktree ownership,) Tj
T*
(test evidence, KMS impact, and deployment boundary. Avoid concurrent edits to) Tj
T*
(shared files; integrate KMS declarations without erasing another pending task.) Tj
T*
(This policy is human/master-conversation orchestration, not an automated scheduler,) Tj
T*
