(# TIS Knowledge Lifecycle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This document defines how the TIS Knowledge Management System evolves with the software from) Tj
T*
(planning through deployment and maintenance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Core Principle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Documentation evolves with implementation. Markdown is the source of truth. The PDF and) Tj
T*
(manifest are generated snapshots. The Knowledge Center is the owner-facing status surface.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(No meaningful implementation is complete until the Knowledge Impact Assessment is complete.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Documentation Lifecycle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. A task is proposed.) Tj
T*
(2. Relevant docs, ADRs, and module history are read.) Tj
T*
(3. The likely documentation impact is identified.) Tj
T*
(4. Implementation happens within approved scope.) Tj
T*
(5. KIA is completed.) Tj
T*
(6. Relevant Markdown docs are updated.) Tj
T*
(7. ADRs are added or updated if decisions changed.) Tj
T*
(8. Module history is updated if a module's documented state changed.) Tj
T*
(9. PDF and manifest are regenerated if included docs changed.) Tj
T*
(10. Final report describes the knowledge impact.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Engineering Lifecycle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Inspect before editing.) Tj
T*
(2. Plan the smallest safe implementation.) Tj
T*
(3. Preserve tenant, identity, permission, SaaS, payment, provisioning, and landing) Tj
T*
(boundaries.) Tj
T*
(4. Implement scoped changes.) Tj
T*
(5. Validate with focused checks.) Tj
T*
(6. Update KMS.) Tj
T*
(7. Report KIA.) Tj
T*
(8. Wait for review, commit, push, or deployment approval.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Approval Lifecycle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Owner defines goal and constraints.) Tj
T*
(2. Implementer confirms scope.) Tj
T*
(3. Implementer makes only approved changes.) Tj
T*
(4. Reviewer checks behavior, scope, docs, validation, and KIA.) Tj
T*
(5. Commit/push/deployment happens only after explicit approval.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Review Lifecycle) Tj
T*
