T*
(- The manifest records documentation version, branch, commit SHA, source paths, mtimes,) Tj
T*
(sizes, and hashes.) Tj
T*
(- The manifest records each included source document's starting PDF page.) Tj
T*
(- The manifest records the generated PDF hash and size.) Tj
T*
(- Markdown source hashes are computed from UTF-8 text normalized to LF, so equivalent CRLF) Tj
T*
(and LF checkouts produce the same hash.) Tj
T*
(- Manifest source paths are repository-relative POSIX paths; dynamically discovered sources) Tj
T*
(use a stable case-insensitive sort with an explicit tie-breaker.) Tj
T*
(- `scripts/generate_docs_pdf.py --check` validates source coverage, titles, approved catalog) Tj
T*
(taxonomy, navigation links, source hashes, PDF identity, manifest metadata, PDF page bounds,) Tj
T*
(and documentation version without writing files.) Tj
T*
(- `kms_catalog.py` is the dependency-free shared vocabulary and path classifier for) Tj
T*
(Knowledge Center presentation and KMS enforcement.) Tj
T*
(- `.kms-impact.yml` records task-level Knowledge Impact in a small machine-readable schema.) Tj
T*
(- `scripts/check_kms_impact.py` classifies likely major changes, validates the declaration) Tj
T*
(against the Git diff, and runs generated-artifact freshness checks.) Tj
T*
(- `scripts/kms.py sync` runs KIA preflight validation, regenerates the PDF and manifest,) Tj
T*
(runs complete freshness validation, and prints a completion summary.) Tj
T*
(- `scripts/kms.py check` is the single read-only validation entry point for local work and) Tj
T*
(CI.) Tj
T*
(- The PDF generator uses ReportLab multi-pass layout to produce a stable table of contents,) Tj
T*
(named source destinations, and document/major-heading outlines without external) Tj
T*
(dependencies.) Tj
T*
(- GitHub Actions enforce KMS checks on pull requests, `dev` pushes, and before `master`) Tj
T*
(deployment.) Tj
T*
(- The Knowledge Center reads the manifest and checks freshness.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Repository owners must configure the `KMS Enforcement / kms-check` status as a required) Tj
T*
(branch-protection check for protected integration branches. Workflow code makes production) Tj
T*
(deployment depend on KMS validation directly; GitHub branch protection is the external) Tj
T*
(setting that makes failed pull requests unmergeable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
