(source_of_truth: true) Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# TIS Knowledge Impact Assessment Standard) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Knowledge Impact Assessment \(KIA\) is a required engineering standard. It confirms) Tj
T*
(whether a task changed project knowledge and whether the KMS was kept current.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Required KIA Fields) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```md) Tj
T*
(Knowledge impact: Yes/No) Tj
T*
(Docs updated:) Tj
T*
(Change history updated: Yes/No) Tj
T*
(ADR needed: Yes/No) Tj
T*
(Module history updated: Yes/No) Tj
T*
(PDF regenerated: Yes/No) Tj
T*
(AI project context updated: Yes/No) Tj
T*
(Reason if not updated:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The same decision must be recorded in `.kms-impact.yml` for machine validation. The) Tj
T*
(repository declaration adds `summary`, `affected_areas`, `kms_files_updated`,) Tj
T*
(`no_impact_reason`, and `major_change_override`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision Tree) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Ask:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Did behavior change?) Tj
T*
(2. Did architecture change?) Tj
T*
(3. Did a workflow change?) Tj
T*
(4. Did a module boundary change?) Tj
T*
(5. Did data ownership or tenant scope change?) Tj
T*
(6. Did SaaS/payment/provisioning change?) Tj
T*
(7. Did UI/UX or customer language change?) Tj
T*
(8. Did roadmap or current state change?) Tj
T*
(9. Did development standards/governance change?) Tj
T*
(10. Would a future developer or AI assistant need to know this?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If any answer is yes, knowledge impact is probably yes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Checklist) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For knowledge-impacting work:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- update relevant source docs,) Tj
T*
(- update `docs/CHANGE_HISTORY.md`,) Tj
T*
(- update module history if module state changed,) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
38 24 Td
(Page 398) Tj
