T*
() Tj
T*
(# ADR 0001: Separate Next.js Landing Website) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Status: Accepted) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date: 2026-06-26) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Context) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(TIS needs a public marketing website and a protected operational application. The public) Tj
T*
(site has different performance, design, routing, and deployment needs than the FastAPI) Tj
T*
(operational portal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Keep the public landing website in `tis-landing-website/` as a separate Next.js app. Keep) Tj
T*
(the FastAPI app as the operational portal at `https://app.tisplatform.com`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Alternatives Considered) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Use FastAPI/Jinja for both marketing and app pages.) Tj
T*
(- Put marketing pages inside the operational app templates.) Tj
T*
(- Use a static site generated outside the repository.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Consequences) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Positive:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Clear separation between marketing and operational concerns.) Tj
T*
(- Landing page can evolve with a modern frontend stack.) Tj
T*
(- Operational FastAPI app remains focused on authenticated workflows.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Tradeoffs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Two runtimes must be understood.) Tj
T*
(- Deployment and routing boundaries must be respected.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
