() Tj
T*
(# ADR 0002: Separate SaaS Identity And Operational Users) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Status: Accepted) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date: 2026-06-26) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Context) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(TIS has SaaS account users who sign up, select plans, onboard organizations, and manage) Tj
T*
(billing. It also has operational tenant users who work inside a provisioned school context.) Tj
T*
(Platform owners and developers are separate platform identities.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Keep SaaS account identity, platform identity, and operational tenant identity distinct.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Alternatives Considered) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Use one user table concept for all public signup, platform, and tenant users.) Tj
T*
(- Automatically convert every SaaS signup into an operational tenant user.) Tj
T*
(- Treat platform users as ordinary tenant administrators.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Consequences) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Positive:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Clearer security boundaries.) Tj
T*
(- Safer tenant isolation.) Tj
T*
(- Billing/onboarding can proceed before operational provisioning.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Tradeoffs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Identity flows require careful documentation.) Tj
T*
(- Developers must avoid mixing account, platform, and tenant assumptions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
