T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
(adr: 0004) Tj
T*
(title: Webhook-Only Payment Confirmation) Tj
T*
(status: Accepted) Tj
T*
(date: 2026-06-26) Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# ADR 0004: Webhook-Only Payment Confirmation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Status: Accepted) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date: 2026-06-26) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Context) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Checkout return pages can be reached by browser redirects, refreshes, or user navigation.) Tj
T*
(They should not be treated as authoritative proof that payment succeeded.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Treat provider webhook confirmation as the authoritative source for successful payment) Tj
T*
(state. Checkout return pages may inform the user but should not independently confirm) Tj
T*
(payment or trigger provisioning as if payment is verified.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The same authority boundary applies to M7 subscription mutations. Local requests and browser) Tj
T*
(submissions are intent, not final financial truth. Webhook processing validates signatures,) Tj
T*
(provider event identity, subscription/customer ownership, expected items/quantity,) Tj
T*
(attributable transactions, and idempotent event state before confirming local outcomes.) Tj
T*
(Ambiguous or mismatched evidence fails closed to manual review.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Initial checkout and post-activation subscription-change lifecycles remain distinct so a) Tj
T*
(completed change transaction cannot accidentally replay initial provisioning/payment) Tj
T*
(transitions. Guarded reconciliation may repair finalized local lifecycle fields only from) Tj
T*
(attributable stored webhook evidence plus authoritative Paddle transaction data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Alternatives Considered) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Confirm payment based on checkout return route.) Tj
T*
(- Allow manual UI confirmation from the SaaS account page.) Tj
T*
(- Provision tenant records immediately after checkout redirect.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Consequences) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Positive:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reduces risk of false-positive payment confirmation.) Tj
T*
(- Aligns billing state with provider-confirmed events.) Tj
T*
(- Supports delayed provisioning after verified payment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Tradeoffs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Users may need clear pending-payment status while webhook processing completes.) Tj
T*
(- Webhook handling must be reliable and observable.) Tj
T*
