(# ADR 0012: Seven-Day Demo Lifecycle And Access Enforcement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Context) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(M8B-4 activates customer-demo workspaces but intentionally defines no expiration. M8B-5) Tj
T*
(requires a standard seven-day lifecycle, a Day 6 reminder, data-preserving expiration, and) Tj
T*
(enforcement that cannot be bypassed by a stale authenticated session or a delayed scheduler.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use `SaaSDemoWorkspaceProvisioning.activated_at` as the only demo clock authority. Persist) Tj
T*
(derived reminder and expiration timestamps for querying, but require the lifecycle resolver) Tj
T*
(to verify that they equal activation plus six and seven days. Perform calculations as) Tj
T*
(timezone-aware UTC values and convert only display values to the onboarding organization's) Tj
T*
(validated IANA timezone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use one read-only resolver for Active, Reminder Due, Expired, Suspended, and Manual Review.) Tj
T*
(Scheduled processing is independently callable, dry-run by default, row-locked, idempotent,) Tj
T*
(and failure-audited. Day 6 creates internal SaaS-account and Platform Owner notifications.) Tj
T*
(Day 7 atomically ends the demo entitlement, suspends the SchoolGroup, marks the demo tenant) Tj
T*
(link expired, and preserves all tenant data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Enforce the same resolver in the existing operational authentication middleware.) Tj
T*
(Customer-demo web requests that are expired or ambiguous are redirected to a subscription) Tj
T*
(activation page; APIs and downloads receive a safe 403. Access-block audit is deduplicated.) Tj
T*
(Platform identities, customer-paid workspaces, internal sandboxes, public/authentication) Tj
T*
(routes, secure logout, and SaaS commercial routes bypass the demo-only gate.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Consequences) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scheduler delay cannot extend demo access because request-time resolution uses the) Tj
T*
(authoritative timestamp.) Tj
T*
(- Existing sessions cannot bypass expiration.) Tj
T*
(- Expiration is reversible by a future approved commercial transition because no tenant data) Tj
T*
(is deleted.) Tj
T*
(- Processing failure rolls back expiration changes and remains safely retryable.) Tj
T*
(- External email, conversion, extension, archive/delete, and read-only expired access remain) Tj
T*
(out of scope.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## M8B7 Amendment) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Day 6 now atomically records the customer notice, Platform Owner Notification Center events,) Tj
T*
(and reminder email intent. Expiry atomically records customer/owner notifications plus) Tj
T*
(expiry and subscription-continuation email intents. Provider delivery occurs outside) Tj
T*
(lifecycle row locks through the durable outbox. The CLI remains dry-run by default and is) Tj
T*
(the Render Cron entry point.) Tj
