(# ADR 0037: Talent Overall Program Result) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Context) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Talent Programs assess one Student across multiple competencies. The Product Owner) Tj
T*
(requires each rubric level to show its ordered numeric rank beside its name and) Tj
T*
(requires one deterministic overall result for the Program Assessment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The canonical result must remain meaningful to educators using the rubric. A) Tj
T*
(Mental Math Program using five ordered levels should therefore report a result) Tj
T*
(such as `4.4 / 5`, rather than replacing the rubric meaning with an invented) Tj
T*
(0-100 score.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Different Talent Programs remain separate assessment domains. Mental Math,) Tj
T*
(Performing Arts, Reading Talent, or future Programs must never be combined into) Tj
T*
(one universal Student Talent score.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Rubric level number) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The canonical numeric rank of a rubric level is its governed ordered position) Tj
T*
(within the competency-owned rubric:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- first level = 1;) Tj
T*
(- second level = 2;) Tj
T*
(- and so on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The UI renders this number directly beside the level name, for example) Tj
T*
(`1. Beginning`, `2. Approaching`, `3. Meets`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The displayed rank is not a second manually-entered score and does not depend on) Tj
T*
(the optional legacy/KPI `numeric_value` field.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### One coherent Program scale) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(All Grade-applicable competency rubrics participating in one completed Student) Tj
T*
(Assessment must use the same number of ordered levels.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For example, if Mental Math is a five-level Program scale, every applicable) Tj
T*
(competency in that Assessment must use five ordered levels.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(TIS must not directly average ranks from incompatible scales such as `4 / 5`) Tj
T*
(and `3 / 3`. An Assessment with inconsistent applicable rubric lengths cannot) Tj
T*
(be completed until the rubric structure is aligned.) Tj
T*
