(SOURCE: docs/history/engineering-handbook/2026-07-21-kms-automatic-enforcement.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
(title: Automatic KMS Synchronization Enforcement) Tj
T*
(module: engineering-handbook) Tj
T*
(date: 2026-07-21) Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# 2026-07-21 - Automatic KMS Synchronization Enforcement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Previous State) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(KMS governance was documented but not mechanically enforced. Developers and AI assistants) Tj
T*
(manually decided impact, edited Markdown, and regenerated artifacts. The Knowledge Center) Tj
T*
(could detect stale hashes, but no pull-request or deployment gate consumed that status.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## New State) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(TIS has a narrow repository enforcement layer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `AGENTS.md` makes KMS onboarding and completion rules default for Codex.) Tj
T*
(- `.kms-impact.yml` records task-level impact, affected areas, updated KMS files, and) Tj
T*
(controlled no-impact overrides.) Tj
T*
(- `scripts/check_kms_impact.py` compares the declaration with a Git range or local worktree,) Tj
T*
(classifies likely major changes, and validates generated artifacts.) Tj
T*
(- `scripts/generate_docs_pdf.py --check` verifies source coverage, source hashes, PDF) Tj
T*
(hash/size, version, and manifest consistency without writing.) Tj
T*
(- GitHub Actions run enforcement for pull requests and `dev`; production deployment from) Tj
T*
(`master` depends on the same gate.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Cross-Platform Correction) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The initial enforcement release exposed two checkout-dependent differences: Markdown hashes) Tj
T*
(reflected raw CRLF/LF bytes, and dynamic source ordering followed native path comparison.) Tj
T*
(The generator and Knowledge Center now hash normalized UTF-8/LF Markdown. The generator also) Tj
T*
(records repository-relative POSIX paths in a deterministic order while continuing to fail on) Tj
T*
(genuine source-list drift. Impact detection includes deleted files so removing behavior or) Tj
T*
(documentation cannot bypass review.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Task-Boundary Correction) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The initial push workflow compared only the previous pushed commit with the new head, while) Tj
T*
(pull requests compared the complete feature branch. Follow-up commits therefore validated a) Tj
T*
(task-level declaration against a commit-level diff. Push checks now derive the task base) Tj
T*
(from the merge base of the default branch and pushed head. Pull-request and push checks) Tj
T*
(consequently enforce the same cumulative KIA scope without allowing undeclared documentation) Tj
T*
(changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Phase 6 Unified Command) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The initial automation exposed generation, artifact checking, and KIA enforcement as) Tj
T*
(separate commands. Phase 6 adds `scripts/kms.py sync` for KIA preflight, PDF/manifest) Tj
T*
(generation, post-generation freshness validation, and completion reporting. `scripts/kms.py) Tj
T*
(check` is the canonical read-only command used locally and by CI. Both commands delegate to) Tj
T*
(the existing generator and checker; they do not duplicate policy or rewrite Markdown.) Tj
T*
ET
BT
